This repository grew out of an assignment for INFO7375 (Semantic Intelligence in
Large Language Models) at Northeastern University.

Provided by the course, not written by me:

  warc_io.py              WARC/WET readers (originally utils.py)
  scripts/download_data.sh
  data/bad_word_list.txt  403 entries
  data/topic_dataset.json 219 single-sentence documents

Everything else -- the extraction, masking, filtering and deduplication logic,
the HuggingFace dataset builder, the census script, the test suite and the
documentation -- is my own work.

The corpus itself is a single WARC shard of the CC-MAIN-2018-17 Common Crawl
dump, distributed by the Common Crawl Foundation under their Terms of Use:
https://commoncrawl.org/terms-of-use
